Cyt c2 HMM frcmod, ferrous state. SHARED across all ferrous charge-set libs (Guberman_HMR_CM5 / _RESPmc / _RESPsc / _CM5_FeLocal) — bonded terms are charge-independent, so one frcmod serves every charge model. Self-complete: macrocycle terms from frcmod.conste (Henriques 2013) with FE→FR fork, Fe-coordination-shell BOND+ANGLE values overridden by our state-specific Seminario fits. No load-time dependence on frcmod.conste. CORRECTED 2026-08-02: the two TRANS pyrrole angles (NP-FR-NP = NA-Fe-NC, NO-FR-NO = NB-Fe-ND) had carried the cis class average 109.99/90.000; re-derived by Seminario from a reproduction of the original ferrous QM — see DESCRIPTION.txt. Trajectories built before this correction are invalid.

MASS
FR  55.85         ! Fe — forked from conste FE for state distinction
NP 14.01
NO 14.01
CD 12.0
Cp 12.010        ! FORKED from CB: heme β-pyrrole carbon (C2A/C3A/C2B/C3B/C2C/C3C/C2D/C3D). parm10 CB is nucleic-acid (CB-CB 520/1.370); heme CB-CB 418/1.357. Fork keeps both. Mirrors b-type heme set.

